IMPORTANT NOTES ON DEPENDENCIES:

This project includes the following licensed components:

1. **Core Engine (LGPL v2.1+)**
   - Your own engine code in Engine/ and Editor/

2. **Dynamically Linked FFmpeg (GPL v2 - External DLL)**
   - FFmpeg is linked as an external dynamic library (.dll on Windows)
   - Users can replace the FFmpeg DLL with their own build
   - FFmpeg source available at: https://ffmpeg.org/

3. **MIT Licensed Libraries:**
   - EnTT, spdlog, Dear ImGui, ImGuizmo, yaml-cpp, stb_image, GLAD, GLM

4. **zlib/BSD Licensed Libraries:**
   - GLFW, Bullet3, tinyfiledialogs

5. **BSD 3-Clause:**
   - Assimp

6. **OpenAL (LGPL/MIT):**
   - OpenAL Soft (dual-licensed)

---

REGARDING COMMERCIAL USE:

Since FFmpeg is linked as a dynamic library (not statically linked),
you may use this software in proprietary/commercial applications with
the following requirements:

1. Distribute the LGPL-licensed engine code with source access or
   dynamic linking capability
2. Allow users to replace the FFmpeg DLL if needed
3. Include this LICENSE file and list of dependencies
4. Attribution to the original authors is appreciated

For questions about licensing compliance, refer to:
- LGPL v2.1: https://www.gnu.org/licenses/lgpl-2.1.html
- FFmpeg licensing: https://ffmpeg.org/legal.html
